From f1c8adea0fbca27b63a2622716ca5113f36061e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rohit Goswami <rgoswami@ieee.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:30:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(fitter): add Fitter.fit_anneal

Runs the anneal drivers through the ChemFit 4 fitter loop. The search starts at initial_params, stays inside bounds (scalar and array leaves, array leaves taking scalar or per-element bounds, so (n_atoms, 3) positions work directly), evaluates the objective at most budget times through evaluate(), calls step() after each evaluation, and returns the best evaluated parameters.

method is portfolio (anneal.global_optimize, default), boltzmann, fast or gsa (anneal.run), or gpmd. Parameters are passed to anneal in the unit cube, so preset steps are in units of each box width. An objective exception stops further evaluations and is re-raised once anneal returns, unless the fitter swallows exceptions. A gradient mapping can be supplied for portfolio and gpmd. anneal is an optional extra; fit_anneal refuses an anneal whose run() lacks x0 and max_evals.
